    "notes": [
      {
        "id": "chicago-rules",
        "heading": "Chicago spells out how a replacement must be connected",
        "text": "In Chicago, the work must be done by the Chicago-licensed plumbing contractor or the homeowner named on the permit. The city's permit terms for replacing a water heater are specific: a listed and labeled unit installed to the maker's instructions, unions at the connections (dielectric ones between different metals), a full-port shutoff on the cold line and no valve on the hot side, and a relief valve outlet that is not piped straight into the drain system.",
        "source": "City of Chicago Department of Buildings, Express Permit Program terms: plumbing work",
        "sourceUrl": "https://www.chicago.gov/city/en/sites/guide-to-building-permits/home/terms-and-conditions/epp/worktype/PLUMB.html",
        "quote": "Plumbing work must be performed by the Chicago-licensed plumbing contractor or homeowner listed on the permit application.",
