    "local": {
      "heading": "What makes an Illinois replacement different",
      "paras": [
        "Illinois is a gas state: 69% of homes heat water with natural gas, and gas is cheap here at $1.07 per therm, so a gas tank costs only about $174 a year to run. That makes a gas-to-gas swap the usual job, and the gas utility rebate is small.",
        "Cold winters shape the tankless choice. Incoming water falls to about 46.8 °F in February, the coldest month, and a whole-house tankless unit then gives about 5.2 gallons per minute. A heat pump tank in an unheated basement can also drop below ENERGY STAR's 40 °F limit in a hard winter, so check the space before you buy one."
      ]
    },
    "highlights": [
      "Illinois's price level matches the U.S. average exactly, so its prices are the national prices; only your metro area moves them.",
      "Natural gas is cheap in Illinois ($1.07 per therm, the 12th lowest of the 50 states and DC), so a gas tank costs only about $174 a year to run, and gas stays the cheapest tank to own over 10 years.",
      "69% of Illinois homes heat water with natural gas, against 48% nationally, so most replacements here are gas-to-gas with an existing vent and gas line.",
      "Where you live inside Illinois matters: the same 50-gallon gas job is about $1,841 in the Chicago-Naperville-Elgin, IL-IN area and $1,729 in the Peoria, IL area.",
      "Chicago spells out how a replacement must be connected."
    ]
